# The plugin's test chain. NOT a digest-pinned input — deliberately. It used to live inside
# package.json's `scripts.test`, which meant every test-adding PR moved the pinned
# `runtimeFiles.pluginPackageJson` hash; two concurrent plugin PRs then conflicted both on that
# one 14 KB line and on the recomputed pin. The list is guarded semantically instead (shape
# allowlist + no shell + bidirectional completeness — see
# plugins/plugin-integration-core/scripts/test-chain.cjs), which is what a digest that legitimately
# moved in every PR could never do.
#
#   eol=lf     — the guards compare chain lines by exact equality; a CRLF checkout would break
#                every one of them. (The parser also strips \r; belt and braces.)
#   merge=union — this is an append-only list, so union is exactly right: two PRs each adding a
#                suite auto-merge and BOTH lines survive, instead of conflicting. A duplicate or a
#                mis-placed line that union could produce is caught by the guards (each suite must
#                appear exactly once; the sealed-export stage tail must remain last).
